# Platform — Chatbot (UC-033, UC-034)
# Guest-only — no actor. TenantContext is populated from X-Tenant-ID (set by the BFF).
#
# Prerequisites:
#   1. pnpm infra:up
#   2. pnpm --filter @ikaro/backend run migration:run
#   3. pnpm --filter @ikaro/backend run seed
#   4. pnpm --filter @ikaro/backend run dev
#
# REST Client environment: select "local" in VS Code status bar

@baseUrl = {{backendUrl}}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# STATUS (UC-034) — pure read, always 200 { available: boolean }
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Available — no cap/health/spend/balance condition currently tripped
GET {{baseUrl}}/platform/chatbot/status
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}

###

### Not available — condition (a): send the same "31+ times" burst from the 429 case below first,
### then re-run this — daily cap already exhausted means status flips to { available: false }
GET {{baseUrl}}/platform/chatbot/status
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}

###

### Not available — condition (c): trigger a real provider failure first (unset/invalid
### OPENROUTER_API_KEY, see the 503 case below), then re-run this within
### CHATBOT_PROVIDER_HEALTH_COOLDOWN_MINUTES (default 5) — half-open cooldown means status stays
### { available: false } until either the cooldown elapses or a subsequent real call succeeds
GET {{baseUrl}}/platform/chatbot/status
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HAPPY PATH
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### New conversation — sessionId omitted, backend creates a new session
POST {{baseUrl}}/platform/chatbot/messages
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "systemPrompt": "You are a helpful assistant for a car wash business. Answer only questions about this business.",
  "message": "Vocês trabalham aos sábados?",
  "clientIp": "203.0.113.10"
}

###

### Existing conversation — sessionId from a prior response's { sessionId, reply }
POST {{baseUrl}}/platform/chatbot/messages
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sessionId": "REPLACE_WITH_SESSION_ID_FROM_PRIOR_RESPONSE",
  "systemPrompt": "You are a helpful assistant for a car wash business. Answer only questions about this business.",
  "message": "E qual o valor da lavagem completa?",
  "clientIp": "203.0.113.10"
}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ERROR CASES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 400 — Missing X-Tenant-ID header
POST {{baseUrl}}/platform/chatbot/messages
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "systemPrompt": "You are a helpful assistant.",
  "message": "Oi",
  "clientIp": "203.0.113.10"
}

###

### 400 — Empty message
POST {{baseUrl}}/platform/chatbot/messages
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "systemPrompt": "You are a helpful assistant.",
  "message": "",
  "clientIp": "203.0.113.10"
}

###

### 404 — sessionId doesn't belong to this tenant (or doesn't exist)
POST {{baseUrl}}/platform/chatbot/messages
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sessionId": "00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000",
  "systemPrompt": "You are a helpful assistant.",
  "message": "Oi",
  "clientIp": "203.0.113.10"
}

###

### 429 — Volume cap reached (send this same request 31+ times in a row for the same
### tenant/day to trigger the default maxConversationsPerDay=30 cap; PLATFORM_CHATBOT_DAILY_CAP_REACHED)
POST {{baseUrl}}/platform/chatbot/messages
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "systemPrompt": "You are a helpful assistant.",
  "message": "Oi",
  "clientIp": "203.0.113.99"
}

###

### 503 — LLM provider call failed (unset/invalid OPENROUTER_API_KEY locally reproduces this;
### PLATFORM_CHATBOT_PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE)
POST {{baseUrl}}/platform/chatbot/messages
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "systemPrompt": "You are a helpful assistant.",
  "message": "Oi",
  "clientIp": "203.0.113.98"
}
